cookbook/references/starter-history-and-knowledge-remain-retrievable.md:25:Keep repository history/license and external source custody when adapting code. Read the scope Decision before changing the trainer, then the relevant port contract; later readers should be able to distinguish intended behavior, source inspection and executed checks. Record every material adaptation, as the owner explicitly requests, with reason, paths, checks and gaps. No v3 empirical Lesson or board exists until results justify it. The setup changes documentation/tooling behavior, not playing strength, CUDA performance or runtime hook trust.
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-teacher-distills-per-slot-kl-and-per-seat-winner-ce.md:3:title: "Kaggriculture teacher distills per-slot KL and per-seat winner CE"
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-teacher-distills-per-slot-kl-and-per-seat-winner-ce.md:4:description: "Phases 4.1-4.3 on CPU: replay-conditioned per-slot masked logits and a liveness-weighted per-slot KL(teacher || student), cached as KaggricultureTeacherTargets (102,208 B per seat row) with a grammar signature, a cached path bit-for-bit equal to the combined path, a live-seat-mean winner CE owned by the model, stateless PPO teacher dispatch and teacher/cache_bytes; eleven killed mutations. Phase 4 is not complete: the trainer and run_ppo launch/resume tests are written but skipped (the launch/resume pair dry-run with config validation bypassed); after the integration merge an unskipped probe still fails all four on the missing Task 3.1 trainer observation mapping and run_ppo's no-env stop (configs and value-mode guards have landed), and 4.4 is not done though its configs prerequisite has merged."
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-teacher-distills-per-slot-kl-and-per-seat-winner-ce.md:51:# Kaggriculture teacher distills per-slot KL and per-seat winner CE
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-teacher-distills-per-slot-kl-and-per-seat-winner-ce.md:61:- `tests/kaggriculture/helpers.py`: the heads tests' tiny models, programs and replay cases, moved unchanged in behavior (65 heads tests pass before and after).
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-teacher-distills-per-slot-kl-and-per-seat-winner-ce.md:64:- `python/owl/model/kaggriculture_teacher.py` (new): `KaggricultureTeacherTargets(slot_logits, winner_probabilities, grammar)` implements `TeacherTargets`. `index` slices dim 0 and carries `grammar`. `concat` validates every chunk symmetrically: optional-field presence, slot keys and grammar must match, and each failure raises `ValueError` naming the field; one chunk is returned without a copy. `nbytes` sums tensor metadata. `GrammarSignature(tables_sha256, hire_limit)` and `TEACHER_TARGET_BYTES_PER_ROW` (102,208, derived from `kt.SLOT_WIDTHS`, 241 unit frames and 11 market positions, plus 8 B of winner probabilities) are also defined there.
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-teacher-distills-per-slot-kl-and-per-seat-winner-ce.md:66:- `python/owl/model/kaggriculture.py`: `grammar_signature()` and `compute_teacher_distillation_targets`, which runs one guarded encode, `_policy(collect_logits=True)`, `check_replay_flags`, a reshape to the lead and the winner probabilities, all under `no_grad`.
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-teacher-distills-per-slot-kl-and-per-seat-winner-ce.md:85:The estimator is Isaiah's: teacher-forced conditionals at the behavior policy's replayed prefix, summed per slot, not an unbiased joint-program KL. Both sides must share the grammar tables and `hire_limit`; replay admission does not detect a mismatch that still admits the program.
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-teacher-distills-per-slot-kl-and-per-seat-winner-ce.md:105:| 4.2 (a) `concat` checks winner presence only against the first chunk | 1 failed (T9) |
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-teacher-distills-per-slot-kl-and-per-seat-winner-ce.md:108:| 4.2 (d) `nbytes` omits winner probabilities | 1 failed (T10) |
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-teacher-distills-per-slot-kl-and-per-seat-winner-ce.md:116:  - **T12:** cached equals combined with `torch.equal` on every field (KL event, per-entity and per-slot components; teacher winner probabilities; student winner log-probs; value CE; student log-probs, entropies and values) for a segment-major batch with a dense row and an inactive seat.
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-teacher-distills-per-slot-kl-and-per-seat-winner-ce.md:117:  - **T13:** a `load_state_dict` copy gives exactly zero KL and the value CE equals the live-seat mean of the student's winner entropy.
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-teacher-distills-per-slot-kl-and-per-seat-winner-ce.md:119:  - **T15:** cached admission rejects Isaiah's target type, missing targets, missing keys, a wrong shape, BF16, a wrong winner shape, a foreign grammar, `hidden_state` and `dones`, all with zero encodes. The combined path rejects an Orbit teacher, a different `action_spec`, different tables and an in-place table edit (same signature), also with zero encodes.
cookbook/decisions/recipe-choices-align-to-isaiah-without-owner-escalation.md:9:sources: [{"resource": "user-directive:2026-09-29:recipe-choices-align-to-isaiah"}, {"resource": "user-directive:2026-09-29:diagnose-bc-and-preserve-training-config"}, {"resource": "user-directive:2026-09-29:scale-environments-keep-ppo-minibatch"}, {"resource": "reference-branch:kg/reference-2026-09-29/ops/isaiah-alignment-2026-09-29/upstream-scaling_6m.yaml"}, {"resource": "reference-branch:kg/reference-2026-09-29/ops/isaiah-alignment-2026-09-29/semantic-audit.json"}, {"resource": "reference-branch:kg/reference-2026-09-29/ops/isaiah-alignment-2026-09-29/results.md"}, {"resource": "reference-branch:kg/reference-2026-09-29/configs/kaggriculture_2rank.yaml"}, {"resource": "reference-branch:kg/reference-2026-09-29/configs/kaggriculture_4rank.yaml"}, {"resource": "reference-branch:kg/reference-2026-09-29/configs/model/kaggriculture.yaml"}, {"resource": "repository:python/owl/train/config.py"}, {"resource": "repository:configs/kaggriculture_2rank.yaml"}, {"resource": "repository:configs/kaggriculture_4rank.yaml"}, {"resource": "repository:scripts/run_ppo.py"}, {"resource": "repository:ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/codex/verify-3.4-r3/report.md"}, {"resource": "external-repository:https://github.com/IsaiahPressman/kaggle-orbit-wars/blob/32b3ec900ad406eedd965f53a1a0f4490d31c589/configs/winner_ce_6m_4x5090.yaml"}, {"resource": "external-repository:https://github.com/IsaiahPressman/kaggle-orbit-wars/blob/32b3ec900ad406eedd965f53a1a0f4490d31c589/python/owl/model/stateless_transformer_v1.py"}]
cookbook/decisions/recipe-choices-align-to-isaiah-without-owner-escalation.md:32:1. **Optimizer-step cadence.** Apply Isaiah's own multi-GPU rule from `winner_ce_6m_4x5090.yaml`: divide `n_envs` and `segments_per_minibatch` by world size, keeping the global batch, 16 optimizer steps/iteration and env steps/iteration of the single-GPU run. For `scaling_6m` (256 envs, spm 16, accumulation 1) this gives 128 envs/rank, spm 8, accumulation 1 on two ranks, and 64/4/1 on four ranks. `target_kl` stays null as upstream. Each iteration then collects 16,384 game transitions and takes 16 optimizer steps of 1,024 global transitions, matching upstream warm-up/cosine data exposure. Residual differences: two-player games only, and dense-game memory is unmeasured, so a memory smoke precedes any long run. Earlier 4,096-env SPS figures do not qualify this cadence.
cookbook/decisions/recipe-choices-align-to-isaiah-without-owner-escalation.md:33:2. **Critic and value distillation.** Upstream `scaling_6m` uses the default softmax winner-distribution critic (value 2p−1, MSE value loss, gamma 1) with a last-best teacher (policy KL 0.005, winner-probability value distillation 0.005). Upstream itself rejects `critic_mode='independent'` with value distillation, so alignment means implementing winner-distribution semantics rather than relaxing that guard. V3 runs one forward per seat-private observation; a critic that combines both seats' private inputs is neither Isaiah's architecture nor required. The nearest analog follows Isaiah's stateless critic: per-player critic value tokens (self and opponent) inside each seat's own observation feed a shared head, giving one logit per player, a softmax and value 2p − 1 (plan Task 3.1). That admits upstream's value distillation without reading the rival's private state. The range check is settled by source: `terminal_scale = 1 - caps` keeps shaped returns in [-1, 1].
cookbook/decisions/recipe-choices-align-to-isaiah-without-owner-escalation.md:37:Current state (implementation status, not owner adoption): target 1 is encoded in the Task 3.4 ranked configs, which load through the real `FullConfig`, and target 2's per-player winner softmax is in the Task 3.1 model ([[../references/kaggriculture-model-joins-isaiahs-factory-compile-and-masked-critic|model-side Reference]]). Native environment and trainer integration, teacher and value-distillation execution, and GPU qualification remain pending, so neither target is yet exercised in training.
cookbook/references/bc-bootstrap-uses-native-replay-features-and-current-heads.md:3:title: "BC bootstrap uses native replay features and current heads"
cookbook/references/bc-bootstrap-uses-native-replay-features-and-current-heads.md:4:description: "Localize zero-bank self-play, prepare exact admitted public actions through Rust, and qualify a separate current-model BC warm start."
cookbook/references/bc-bootstrap-uses-native-replay-features-and-current-heads.md:11:# BC bootstrap uses native replay features and current heads
cookbook/references/bc-bootstrap-uses-native-replay-features-and-current-heads.md:15:The current policy and initial incumbent both end at zero banks in8 native games/seeds7000–7007,16 seat trajectories each. Current-policy mean bank falls from3000 to595.125 after one turn,26.5625 after eight, and zero by192; the initial policy shows the same failure pattern. Removing market orders while retaining model unit commands preserves3000 for every seat through719 turns, as does full PASS. This localizes the observed cash depletion to market behavior rather than a zeroed bank metric. It does not establish an optimal no-trade policy or full engine correctness. Diagnostic action sampling is eager BF16, not a compiled-path numerical parity or speed test.
cookbook/references/bc-bootstrap-uses-native-replay-features-and-current-heads.md:17:Both-zero terminal W/L/D gives no ranking signal between these policies. Econ.2 is a capped death-potential difference, not a penalty for arbitrary spending or a bank-profit target. The current-policy diagnostic also accumulates8193 ineffective unit commands; economic production chains remain unlearned. Prior cookbook search found no qualified v3 BC implementation; v2's public replay loader provides observation/action alignment and shared-field semantics, not its model, collector or training code.
cookbook/references/bc-bootstrap-uses-native-replay-features-and-current-heads.md:23:- `ops/bc-bootstrap-2026-09-29/select_replays.py`, `prepare.py`: read-only source volume4llk4uaf20, source days09-21..27, seeded32 training and4 validation episodes/day.252 episodes are split by identity, with duplicate episode basenames rejected in preparation. Hash each source payload and prepared shard. Pair observation[t] with action[t+1], fill seat1 schema-shared fields, and preserve own-private encoding. Omitted units are filled with Python `None`, which `actor_codec._unit_frame` rejects; the earlier claim that they become explicit NONE was incorrect. Never truncate market orders or quantities. Replay JSON is processed once offline; resident GPU arrays feed BC minibatches. The [[rebuild-data-preparation-preserves-replay-identity|rebuild Reference]] records the source check and v4 admission consequence; this correction does not alter the historical manifest counts.
cookbook/references/bc-bootstrap-uses-native-replay-features-and-current-heads.md:24:- `train_bc.py`: current8,353,727-parameter stateless v3 actor; no v2 weights/model or opponent identity. Reuse current evaluate_actions, compiler, BF16, distributed context and optimizer factory. Mean turn NLL is normalized by active frame count; frozen critic head receives no supervised value target, but shared-trunk updates still change its predictions. Two ranks use64 game rows/128 seat observations per microbatch, accumulation2 and512-seat global optimizer batch. Fresh AdamW state, learning rate1e-4, weight decay.01. This is offline BC, not a second PPO trainer. Validation uses a fixed random subset of held-out episode rows and selects best NLL; it is neither final playing strength nor a promotion.
cookbook/references/bc-bootstrap-uses-native-replay-features-and-current-heads.md:25:- `evaluate_bc.py`, `run.sh`, `disable-automatic-ppo`: the75-minute BC run is independent. The owner corrected the earlier automatic-PPO interpretation. The launcher now ends after BC; a remotely verified exit2 guard prevents the already-running wrapper from entering its buffered PPO path. This intentional handoff exit is separate from the BC trainer exit code. Launch manifests remain frozen; changed file hashes and verification are in `handoff-cancellation.json`.
cookbook/references/bc-bootstrap-uses-native-replay-features-and-current-heads.md:29:The252-episode slice admits158,772 paired turns (139,835 training;18,937 validation) and rejects22,416/181,188 turns (12.37%). Rejection counts:unknown market command14,007; unsupported unit arguments5621; market-item mask1668; extra hand commands1102; queue limit17; quantity range1. A12-episode inspection identifies `INVALID` market markers among rejected commands. Rejections can bias phase/action coverage; no claim that this slice represents all v2 BC data. Both seats are used without outcome filtering; episode split alone does not prove opponent-general holdout.
cookbook/references/bc-bootstrap-uses-native-replay-features-and-current-heads.md:31:Eager two-rank smoke passes8 updates/4096 seat turns with validation NLL3.648→3.575 on two episodes. Full-data compiled two-rank smoke passes8 updates/4096 seat turns with NLL3.925→3.853. Independent checks confirm finite updated actor weights, unchanged critic-head tensors and canonical checkpoint key compatibility. Cold smoke throughput is not a sustained BC benchmark. The original smoke checkpoint metadata included BC-only keys; the harness was corrected and rerun before launch so weights-only handoff uses the canonical schema, with BC metadata in separate artifacts.
cookbook/references/bc-bootstrap-uses-native-replay-features-and-current-heads.md:33:BC quality remains unqualified: the fixed held-out subset NLL reaches0.761 at14,600 updates, then degrades to1.954 at75,600 while training loss falls. This is overfitting on the selected corpus; longer runtime alone does not establish improvement. Best weights are retained. Full held-out evaluation, action-level fidelity and free-running economic behavior remain unverified. The owner subsequently requests a separate half-hour PPO from BC best; BC is stopped early for that switch, so there is no completed75-minute BC result. The separate launch is documented in `ops/ppo-from-bc-2026-09-29/plan.md`. It failed: after 3 iterations and only 6 optimizer steps (KL 1.8894/1.0453/0.3651; win rates 12.5/10.55/3.52% against the BC incumbent), rollout hit a CUDA illegal memory access and rank 1 then hit the 600 s NCCL timeout. A later blocking reproduction traced it to a compiler-generated GEMM overflow on the 8,192-row rollout forward, which also corrupted rollout activations. The KL spikes and falling win rates are therefore not evidence against the BC policy ([[compiled-gemm-template-overflows-above-2-21-rows|compiler overflow Reference]]). No final checkpoint exists; the BC best and its pre-PPO copy have matching SHA-256. Automatic handoff remains disabled. The planned Isaiah alignment changes the architecture (per-player critic value tokens, possibly model size), so it schedules one BC rerun (`ops/gap-closure-2026-09-29/plan.md`, Phase 4). Preserve the [[../decisions/preserve-the-ppo-recipe-across-bc-bootstrap|PPO recipe]]; do not infer readiness or promotion from these local-loss smoke checks.
cookbook/references/live-differential-parity-checks-the-rust-kernel.md:106:framework behavior outside the interpreter is not modeled. The 40-game, 303-probe
cookbook/references/full-turn-intentions-coordinate-batched-action-heads.md:26:behavior. Distinguishable actors can choose complementary actions from the same
cookbook/references/reward-reuse-preserves-objective-and-critic-semantics.md:42:Owner asks “你有沒有加econ shaping (0.2)?” before the half-hour run. The preceding verification run used unshaped terminal W/L/D; implementation availability did not mean it was enabled. Both GPU recipes now explicitly use W=.2, starvation/drought weights4/1, death cap.25, ineffective weight0, gamma1 and terminal scale.75. The .2 value is the event coefficient, not the cap or an extra own-bank bonus. Bank-based evaluation/promotion remains unchanged. A bounded two-GPU run confirmed nonzero shaping (max step reward .25, zero-sum mean 0); its receipt is `ops/default4096-2026-09-29/results.md`. That establishes execution, not learning benefit. The Isaiah-aligned critic (per-player winner softmax, value 2p − 1) is compatible with this recipe because `terminal_scale = 1 - caps` keeps returns in [-1, 1].
cookbook/references/failed-training-reports-status-before-distributed-cleanup.md:46:  the behavior; the task brief and result receipt retain the local evidence.
cookbook/references/ppo-trainer-seams-map-any-schema-and-alarm-on-replay-drift.md:62:- `docs/model-architecture.md` describes the protocol. It and the docstrings state the inherited `concat` behavior exactly: the first chunk's layout wins, a later chunk missing one of its optional targets raises, and a target carried only by later chunks is silently dropped. `python/owl/model/base.py` is untouched because another stream owns it.
cookbook/references/ppo-trainer-seams-map-any-schema-and-alarm-on-replay-drift.md:83:- **Phase 4 prep:** index matches direct slicing, and index-then-concat is exact for five optional-target layouts and three chunk sizes. Both chunk orders are pinned for action params, continuation logits and winner probabilities: a later chunk missing a target raises, while a first chunk missing it drops the later chunk's target.
cookbook/references/ppo-trainer-seams-map-any-schema-and-alarm-on-replay-drift.md:93:- **Concat asymmetry kept for Orbit only.** `CachedTeacherDistillationTargets.concat` still raises when a later chunk lacks an optional target that the first chunk has, and silently drops a target that only later chunks carry; tests pin both orders. Phase 4 kept this inherited rule, because the trainer never builds mixed chunks and Codex's brief review accepted it. The new `KaggricultureTeacherTargets.concat` validates symmetrically ([[kaggriculture-teacher-distills-per-slot-kl-and-per-seat-winner-ce|Phase 4 teacher Reference]]).
cookbook/references/ppo-trainer-seams-map-any-schema-and-alarm-on-replay-drift.md:94:- **Trainer typing is protocol-based.** Since Phase 4.2, `BaseModelAPI`, `ppo.py` and the DDP adapter type the cached-teacher API by `TeacherTargets`, and each model narrows with `isinstance` and raises `TypeError` for foreign targets. The protocol also gained `nbytes()` for `teacher/cache_bytes` ([[kaggriculture-teacher-distills-per-slot-kl-and-per-seat-winner-ce|Phase 4 teacher Reference]]).
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-bc-trainer-warm-starts-ppo-from-the-held-out-best.md:3:title: "Kaggriculture BC trainer warm-starts PPO from the held-out best"
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-bc-trainer-warm-starts-ppo-from-the-held-out-best.md:4:description: "Task 5.2 trainer script: scripts/train_bc.py trains the registered KaggricultureTransformer on teacher-forced replay NLL plus a winner cross-entropy critic target from raw final banks, through Isaiah's factory, optimizer, BF16 autocast, cuBLAS-only compile and DDP seams. It reads the refreshed 5.1 kaggriculture-bc-shard-v1 format into rank-partitioned host memory, keeps every strict held-out-NLL minimum as the best checkpoint in run_ppo's exact schema, stops after sustained non-improvement beyond min_delta over scheduled evaluations (L9), and records each resume as a new attempt with its own source under an unchanged trajectory config. CPU-tested with synthetic shards; no GPU, DDP, compile, real-data or W&B execution yet."
