Location: scripts/kaggriculture_prepare_bc.py:779-784; current invocation custody is published at :793-819.
Records are loaded solely by day/episode filename. Their source hash, source/code identity, split and stride are not compared with the current task. A resumed run can therefore keep old labels/winner masks while presenting the current source/config as its dataset origin. This can also retain outputs from before a pairing correction.
Reproduction: prepared the two original local episodes; copied only episode 114406062's completed record and shard into a scratch incomplete output; changed only its terminal banks in a scratch copy of the source ZIP to exchange the winner; invoked the same CLI with that scratch source. The CLI reported 1 done/1 to do and exited 0. Current source banks were [42478,7213] (winner 0), but the newly published manifest and successfully loaded trainer batch retained [7213,42478] and policy_seat [false,true] (winner 1). Source hashes differ. See resume-result.json and resume.log. Original source files were not modified.
Fix: persist and validate preparation/source/options identity before reusing completed records; reject or rebuild mismatched episodes. This is one resume correctness issue, not proof of actual train/validation overlap. Same-input resume is covered by the passing test.

P3 — CLI default dates are still 21-27 rather than owner-requested 22-28.
Location: scripts/kaggriculture_prepare_bc.py:718 (also module text :4).
Explicit --days 22-28 works. Align the default/help text to avoid an accidental wrong window.

